WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
Rwanda, 1994.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.650
About 85 per cent of the people were Hutu,

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.970
14 per cent Tutsi and 1 per cent Twa.

4
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:13.050
A Hutu-dominated government faced
the Rwandan Patriotic Front,

5
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.870
mainly Tutsi exiles.

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.870
The RPF had invaded from Uganda in 1990.

7
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.950
Conflict can range from protest to war,
and most cases have several causes acting

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:24.930
together.

9
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.910
So why do some tensions
end in a peace deal,

10
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.370
and others in war or division?

11
00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.590
Is it how old the hatred is?

12
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.470
In this mission, you'll see what happens
when one ethnic group dominates the state.

13
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.710
Then you'll compare real cases, and
judge what makes the difference.

14
00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: explain why ethnic
tensions end so differently.
